WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.400 --> 00:11.540
- Hello. - I'm sorry.

3
00:11.540 --> 00:14.090
What? Why?

4
00:15.590 --> 00:19.440
I thought you would accuse me of slacking.

5
00:20.270 --> 00:21.840
No, of course not.

6
00:21.840 --> 00:25.490
Taking breaks is important.

7
00:27.340 --> 00:29.420
What were you up to?

8
00:32.880 --> 00:35.930
A flowerbed, here?

9
00:35.930 --> 00:38.640
- I never noticed. - Yes, well,

10
00:38.640 --> 00:41.990
I saw it from the music room.

11
00:41.990 --> 00:44.920
My guess is that the janitor planted these.

12
00:44.920 --> 00:47.650
By the way, Ms. Nashiki.

13
00:47.650 --> 00:49.530
What club activity do you supervise?

14
00:49.530 --> 00:51.330
I manage the chorus club.

15
00:51.330 --> 00:53.630
The other clubs are a bit much for me.

16
00:53.630 --> 00:57.080
I see. Chorus, huh?

17
00:57.080 --> 01:00.460
Must be nice, not having to attend sports matches.

18
01:01.680 --> 01:04.130
We have recitals instead.

19
01:05.070 --> 01:06.550
- Right. - Yes.

20
01:06.550 --> 01:08.200
Sorry.

21
01:09.060 --> 01:14.300
♪ Dost we dance or sing? ♪

22
01:14.300 --> 01:18.190
♪ Or do we come to see Tokubei's wife on the isle? ♪

23
01:18.190 --> 01:24.440
♪ Three and a four, and a three, and a four ♪

24
01:25.930 --> 01:27.660
That's our current song.

25
01:30.550 --> 01:32.550
What a strange tune.

26
01:32.550 --> 01:34.030
I agree.

27
01:35.630 --> 01:39.780
♪ Dost we dance or sing? ♪

28
01:39.780 --> 01:42.800
♪ Or do we come to see Tokubei's wife on the isle? ♪

29
01:42.800 --> 01:47.790
♪ Three and a four, and a three, and a four ♪

30
01:47.790 --> 01:50.910
♪ Dost we dance or sing? ♪

31
01:50.910 --> 01:53.060
Sir?

32
01:54.800 --> 01:57.410
Strange guy.

33
02:00.150 --> 02:02.330
Get off, this is our stop.

34
02:09.300 --> 02:11.210
Thank you.

35
02:17.240 --> 02:19.400
Where is this?

36
02:22.050 --> 02:23.230
A castle?

37
02:23.230 --> 02:27.370
This is no castle. Come on...

38
02:27.370 --> 02:29.730
- Ow... - I'm an unlucky guy.

39
02:29.730 --> 02:32.780
I'm confident I'm the unluckiest dude around.

40
02:32.780 --> 02:34.250
What the...

41
02:34.250 --> 02:37.490
What a beautiful orb.

42
02:37.490 --> 02:40.230
Is it agate or quartz?

43
02:43.520 --> 02:45.490
No! You'll break...

44
02:49.910 --> 02:51.280
Let's go.

45
02:51.280 --> 02:53.160
Hold on a second.

46
02:53.160 --> 02:55.570
The hell is that? A mechanical orb?

47
02:55.570 --> 02:58.340
No, it's a child's forgotten toy. We'll leave it here.

48
02:58.340 --> 02:59.990
Just one more time, please?

49
02:59.990 --> 03:02.780
That bounced like crazy!

50
03:02.780 --> 03:06.290
Keep your voice down! It's night time.

51
03:10.370 --> 03:15.120
Not only am I unlucky, but now I've got some insane baggage.

52
03:15.940 --> 03:17.770
Ms. Nashiki, your hand.

53
03:27.030 --> 03:28.200
Ms. Nashiki!

54
03:28.200 --> 03:30.540
Who's this "Ms. Nashiki" you keep talking about?

55
03:30.540 --> 03:32.950
I'm Iroha, daughter to the Tokubei Couriers.

56
03:32.950 --> 03:34.370
I have no surname!

57
03:34.370 --> 03:38.990
I'll become the teacher she wanted to be.

58
03:41.140 --> 03:42.170
This is awful.

59
03:42.170 --> 03:43.620
What the heck?

60
03:43.620 --> 03:46.100
This is awesome!

61
03:46.100 --> 03:49.910
Like cherry blossom colored snowflakes!

62
03:49.910 --> 03:54.830
Will she change my fate? Or...

63
04:01.850 --> 04:03.980
Yeah, not happening.

64
04:03.980 --> 04:06.790
Shush! Be quiet!

65
04:06.790 --> 04:08.660
- Come on. - Yeah.

66
04:08.660 --> 04:10.460
Leave it behind.

67
04:12.010 --> 04:13.580
We're heading in.

68
04:22.600 --> 04:26.030
[Episode 2]

69
04:32.850 --> 04:35.990
You damned specter.

70
04:35.990 --> 04:37.920
I will end you where you stand!

71
04:37.920 --> 04:39.680
My words exactly.

72
04:39.680 --> 04:43.460
For I have returned as a wandering phantom.

73
04:58.620 --> 05:01.620
What the heck? I almost cleared that stage!

74
05:01.620 --> 05:03.420
- You're the worst. - Saya.

75
05:03.420 --> 05:05.840
I told you no playing games all day.

76
05:05.840 --> 05:08.080
Busybody.

77
05:10.760 --> 05:12.620
- Uh, who's this? - Don't mind her.

78
05:12.620 --> 05:14.900
Of course I'm going to mind.

79
05:14.900 --> 05:17.030
- Who is she? - Hey.

80
05:17.030 --> 05:18.430
Those people...

81
05:18.430 --> 05:21.500
You've never brought over a guest.

82
05:21.500 --> 05:23.090
- Is she your girlfriend? - No.

83
05:23.090 --> 05:26.020
Hey, where did those people go?

84
05:26.020 --> 05:27.580
Hello?

85
05:28.320 --> 05:29.830
Huh?

86
05:33.780 --> 05:35.020
I died.

87
05:35.020 --> 05:36.740
[GAME OVER]

88
05:36.740 --> 05:38.620
She died?

89
05:40.240 --> 05:41.660
Damn samurai.

90
05:41.660 --> 05:44.740
Always desecrating people's lives.

91
05:44.740 --> 05:47.640
- How do I get in here? - Woah...

92
05:47.640 --> 05:49.450
- Hey! - Is she okay in the head?

93
05:49.450 --> 05:51.180
- Can you hear me? - That's enough.

94
05:51.180 --> 05:54.290
Anyone? Help!

95
05:54.290 --> 05:56.870
Forget all that. No one is dead.

96
05:56.870 --> 05:57.970
Huh?

97
05:57.970 --> 05:59.190
Let me introduce you two.

98
05:59.190 --> 06:01.730
This is Iroha Nashiki. She'll be staying at our place.

99
06:01.730 --> 06:03.330
What? Why?

100
06:03.330 --> 06:04.800
And this is my younger sister, Saya.

101
06:04.800 --> 06:07.710
Your younger sister?

102
06:09.680 --> 06:11.820
What an absolute doll.

103
06:11.820 --> 06:13.240
"D-Doll"?

104
06:13.240 --> 06:15.100
Don't mind her language.

105
06:17.420 --> 06:19.640
Hey. I said, hey!

106
06:19.640 --> 06:22.860
You're in there, aren't you? Hey!

107
06:22.860 --> 06:24.770
You alright?

108
06:28.870 --> 06:29.960
- Hello? - Ikuru.

109
06:29.960 --> 06:31.920
Ikuru!

110
06:31.920 --> 06:34.330
Can I get an explanation?

111
06:34.330 --> 06:37.730
- It'll get a bit long... - Hey.

112
06:37.730 --> 06:39.750
Where is this?

113
06:39.750 --> 06:41.480
Huh?

114
06:41.480 --> 06:43.210
What do you mean, "where"?

115
06:43.210 --> 06:45.980
This place, it looks like my village.

116
06:45.980 --> 06:48.280
Well...

117
06:56.190 --> 06:57.920
Alright.

118
06:57.920 --> 07:00.640
- Follow me. - Right.

119
07:00.640 --> 07:02.310
This is the washroom.

120
07:02.310 --> 07:03.890
Okay.

121
07:03.890 --> 07:06.100
I'll leave out a towel for you.

122
07:07.990 --> 07:09.970
Missus Saya...

123
07:09.970 --> 07:11.640
Yeah?

124
07:11.640 --> 07:13.250
This thing...

125
07:14.050 --> 07:15.800
Our mirror?

126
07:15.800 --> 07:20.820
She really looks exactly like me.

127
07:20.820 --> 07:22.720
Well, it is your own face.

128
07:22.720 --> 07:27.210
I've never seen it so clearly before.

129
07:27.210 --> 07:32.600
I only see it when I go to the well, or the hairdresser.

130
07:34.130 --> 07:40.060
It sure does feel strange, not having my hair up.

131
07:40.060 --> 07:41.630
Huh? R-Right...

132
07:44.910 --> 07:47.050
- Anyway, here. - Thanks.

133
07:47.050 --> 07:49.690
Huh? The hell is this?

134
07:49.690 --> 07:52.110
It's so fluffy!

135
07:52.110 --> 07:54.390
Hey! Hey!

136
07:54.390 --> 07:56.640
What is this? It's so...

137
07:57.740 --> 07:59.680
What're you doing?

138
08:04.710 --> 08:06.440
Here you go.

139
08:08.150 --> 08:11.330
Did you make this?

140
08:11.330 --> 08:12.580
Yeah.

141
08:12.580 --> 08:14.460
In that short amount of time?

142
08:18.200 --> 08:20.090
Thank you.

143
08:20.090 --> 08:22.010
No problem.

144
08:47.910 --> 08:49.700
You...

145
08:49.700 --> 08:51.730
I mean.

146
08:51.730 --> 08:53.860
Master Ichinose.

147
08:54.450 --> 08:57.790
To think you had such talents.

148
09:01.190 --> 09:03.520
- Ikuru. - I know.

149
09:03.520 --> 09:05.410
I'll explain after I eat.

150
09:06.040 --> 09:09.270
This ain't soba, or udon.

151
09:09.270 --> 09:13.750
Hell, I bet not even the shogun has eaten something like this!

152
09:13.750 --> 09:16.730
But to see a man,

153
09:16.730 --> 09:20.090
standing in the kitchen?

154
09:21.020 --> 09:23.340
That's nothing unheard of.

155
09:23.340 --> 09:24.380
What?

156
09:24.380 --> 09:27.680
Yeah, anyone can whip up something like this.

157
09:27.680 --> 09:31.370
Is that why women can be teachers too?

158
09:31.370 --> 09:32.740
Of course.

159
09:32.740 --> 09:34.730
No one's restricted to a job.

160
09:34.730 --> 09:36.370
That's nothing to take for granted.

161
09:36.370 --> 09:39.200
To be able to choose a job...

162
09:39.200 --> 09:42.400
Normally, your job is dictated by family lineage.

163
09:42.400 --> 09:46.370
Samurai will be samurai. Commoners will be commoners.

164
09:46.370 --> 09:48.640
Since my family runs a courier business,

165
09:48.640 --> 09:53.050
my father was disappointed to have a baby girl.

166
09:54.370 --> 09:56.950
Who is Iroha, really?

167
09:56.950 --> 09:59.540
She speaks like an Edo era NPC.

168
10:00.170 --> 10:04.350
Right. I've never heard of this "Edo era",

169
10:04.350 --> 10:07.030
but where I was from, it was Jokyo 2 (1685).

170
10:07.030 --> 10:10.410
- Jokyo 2? - Jokyo 2...

171
10:10.410 --> 10:12.460
That was...

172
10:12.460 --> 10:13.670
No way.

173
10:13.670 --> 10:15.900
She's a time traveler?

174
10:16.940 --> 10:19.830
- So next thing you knew, you were here? - Yeah.

175
10:19.830 --> 10:22.690
Then where's the original Iroha Nashiki?

176
10:22.690 --> 10:25.860
- Who knows. - Seriously?

177
10:25.860 --> 10:27.740
Saya, grab the cups for me.

178
10:27.740 --> 10:30.370
Ikuru! This is no time for washing dishes!

179
10:30.370 --> 10:32.580
Someone has to clean up.

180
10:32.580 --> 10:35.860
Hold on. Let me get the facts straight.

181
10:35.860 --> 10:39.160
First, what triggered her time traveling?

182
10:39.910 --> 10:42.130
Was it the comet tonight?

183
10:42.930 --> 10:44.640
Okay, theory one.

184
10:44.640 --> 10:48.860
Modern Iroha and Edo Iroha swapped places.

185
10:48.860 --> 10:50.110
Theory two.

186
10:50.110 --> 10:53.610
Edo Iroha is Modern Iroha's ancestor, and they synced up.

187
10:53.610 --> 10:55.350
"Sync"?

188
10:55.350 --> 11:01.790
Theory three. Modern Iroha's life force was weakened,

189
11:01.790 --> 11:03.270
so Edo Iroha took over.

190
11:03.270 --> 11:04.530
Took over?

191
11:04.530 --> 11:09.030
That makes me sound like a ghost...

192
11:09.030 --> 11:10.340
Just so we're sure,

193
11:10.340 --> 11:13.860
Modern Iroha isn't dead or anything, right?

194
11:13.860 --> 11:16.090
Of course not...

195
11:18.550 --> 11:21.640
Of course...

196
11:21.640 --> 11:22.640
Not...

197
11:22.640 --> 11:26.230
What if I were a ghost?

198
11:26.230 --> 11:32.460
What if I committed murder?

199
11:33.350 --> 11:35.250
Get a grip!

200
11:35.250 --> 11:36.630
- Ikuru. - What?

201
11:36.630 --> 11:38.180
You too, Iroha.

202
11:38.180 --> 11:39.810
- Huh? - Stand up. Come on.

203
11:39.810 --> 11:40.810
Saya!

204
11:40.810 --> 11:42.920
You traveled through time.

205
11:42.920 --> 11:46.540
Meaning only your soul came to this modern era.

206
11:46.540 --> 11:49.770
Let's blame it on a bug in the space-time continuum.

207
11:49.770 --> 11:51.430
A bug?

208
11:51.430 --> 11:54.030
In other words, you'll find your way home eventually.

209
11:54.920 --> 11:57.730
Realistically speaking, that's not possible.

210
11:57.730 --> 12:00.250
I'd rather blame it all on stress.

211
12:00.250 --> 12:02.850
Face the facts, Ikuru.

212
12:02.850 --> 12:06.240
You've watched "Back to the Future". "The Girl Who Leapt Through Time"?

213
12:06.240 --> 12:07.880
Those are both works of fiction.

214
12:07.880 --> 12:10.670
You'll be able to go home, promise.

215
12:10.670 --> 12:12.140
Really?

216
12:12.140 --> 12:14.200
You can't be absolutely certain.

217
12:14.200 --> 12:16.740
The last time we saw that comet was 341 years ago.

218
12:16.740 --> 12:20.090
If that was the trigger, when will it happen next?

219
12:20.890 --> 12:24.170
So, this "comet".

220
12:24.170 --> 12:26.880
Even if it doesn't come,

221
12:26.880 --> 12:31.260
maybe I'll be pushed out if this girl starts wanting to live?

222
12:32.530 --> 12:34.030
I mean,

223
12:34.030 --> 12:38.480
this body is her's, right?

224
12:38.480 --> 12:41.560
So if her own soul returns...

225
12:41.560 --> 12:43.120
You make a point.

226
12:43.120 --> 12:46.250
If Modern Iroha is only unconscious,

227
12:46.250 --> 12:49.400
then she'll likely revive once her vitality is restored.

228
12:49.400 --> 12:50.590
We have no time.

229
12:50.590 --> 12:52.850
Once Golden Week is over, school is back in session.

230
12:52.850 --> 12:55.800
Let's hope she comes back after a night's rest.

231
12:55.800 --> 13:01.080
♪ Dost we dance or sing? ♪

232
13:03.580 --> 13:06.070
- Ikuru. - What?

233
13:06.070 --> 13:08.510
Did you like Ms. Nashiki?

234
13:08.510 --> 13:09.700
- What? - Is that true?

235
13:09.700 --> 13:11.650
No! No, no, no!

236
13:11.650 --> 13:14.520
I barely even spoke to her!

237
13:14.520 --> 13:17.190
Aw, boring.

238
13:17.190 --> 13:19.370
Boring.

239
13:19.370 --> 13:22.000
[Iroha Nashiki]

240
13:31.690 --> 13:34.060
That looks great on you, Ms. Iroha.

241
13:34.060 --> 13:36.420
I'm glad Mom's old yukata fit you.

242
13:36.420 --> 13:38.450
Thanks.

243
13:39.710 --> 13:41.990
What? Woah! What's that?

244
13:41.990 --> 13:43.590
What is it?

245
13:43.590 --> 13:45.850
- Turn around. - Okay?

246
13:45.850 --> 13:47.690
Huh?

247
13:47.690 --> 13:49.260
Okay, ready?

248
13:53.120 --> 13:55.380
It's warm!

249
13:55.380 --> 13:58.790
- Right? - I get it now.

250
13:59.550 --> 14:03.690
What will you do if Ms. Nashiki doesn't return?

251
14:03.690 --> 14:05.920
Will you be a teacher in her stead?

252
14:05.920 --> 14:08.970
Yeah, that's the plan.

253
14:09.630 --> 14:10.970
Right, the textbooks.

254
14:10.970 --> 14:13.860
I borrowed her textbooks.

255
14:13.860 --> 14:17.470
So long as I have these...

256
14:17.470 --> 14:19.340
[Circles and spheres]

257
14:29.350 --> 14:30.590
[Mr. Sun's Soup]

258
14:30.590 --> 14:32.390
I can't read a word.

259
14:34.200 --> 14:35.930
Missus Saya.

260
14:35.930 --> 14:38.620
May I ask you to teach me?

261
14:40.070 --> 14:41.810
Alright.

262
14:41.810 --> 14:44.120
Let's cram this information into your noggin.

263
14:44.120 --> 14:45.660
Yes, ma'am!

264
14:47.900 --> 14:51.020
[Iroha Nashiki, Accident]

265
14:59.320 --> 15:00.520
Ms. Nashiki.

266
15:00.520 --> 15:05.070
A parent called requesting to reschedule their parent-teacher conference.

267
15:06.280 --> 15:10.130
I already did, three times.

268
15:10.130 --> 15:13.680
I suppose it happens. Especially when both parents are working.

269
15:13.680 --> 15:17.500
I had them swap time slots with another family.

270
15:17.500 --> 15:21.270
Sometimes the changes are a domino effect.

271
15:21.270 --> 15:23.310
What an absolute pain.

272
15:24.670 --> 15:27.640
Huh? Are you alright?

273
15:27.640 --> 15:29.320
It's just a rescheduling, right?

274
15:29.320 --> 15:30.860
- Are you okay? - Ms. Nashiki?

275
15:30.860 --> 15:33.390
- I'm sorry. - Are you feeling dizzy?

276
15:33.390 --> 15:34.810
Excuse us.

277
15:34.810 --> 15:37.160
- Huh? Where's Morikawa? - We're almost there.

278
15:37.160 --> 15:38.570
- Not here? - They must've left.

279
15:38.570 --> 15:40.300
I see.

280
15:40.300 --> 15:41.560
Let's have you lie down first.

281
15:41.560 --> 15:42.800
Okay.

282
15:42.800 --> 15:46.150
Ms. Sakurai. To the principal's office, please.

283
15:46.150 --> 15:47.460
- I'm being called. - I'll take over.

284
15:47.460 --> 15:48.750
Thank you.

285
15:48.750 --> 15:51.380
- Go on, you're almost there. - Sorry.

286
15:51.380 --> 15:53.230
And you, try not to touch her.

287
15:53.230 --> 15:54.360
- Yes, ma'am. - Thank you.

288
15:54.360 --> 15:56.320
Ms. Nashiki, take my arm.

289
15:56.320 --> 15:58.290
I'm fine.

290
15:59.920 --> 16:01.860
- Thank you. - Here.

291
16:05.580 --> 16:08.590
- I'll help. - Thank you.

292
16:13.240 --> 16:15.010
The medicine...

293
16:17.640 --> 16:19.900
Which one is the right one?

294
16:20.770 --> 16:24.910
I already took medicine for my stomach earlier.

295
16:25.560 --> 16:27.390
Sorry.

296
16:35.600 --> 16:37.730
When did this start?

297
16:38.960 --> 16:43.450
It's only been two weeks since the school year began.

298
16:47.330 --> 16:48.840
I'm sorry.

299
16:48.840 --> 16:50.580
I'm not accusing you.

300
16:50.580 --> 16:53.550
But you shouldn't push yourself.

301
16:53.550 --> 16:57.220
I won't cause trouble.

302
16:58.670 --> 17:00.320
Should I tell the principal?

303
17:00.320 --> 17:03.530
So we have back-up if something happens...

304
17:05.390 --> 17:10.050
I won't ever cause trouble again.

305
17:13.410 --> 17:15.230
Okay.

306
17:16.250 --> 17:18.640
Thank you.

307
17:40.650 --> 17:43.200
Ms. Iroha fell asleep.

308
17:44.100 --> 17:47.780
What're you going to do about her?

309
17:48.780 --> 17:54.530
She has a house, and an ID at the very least.

310
17:54.530 --> 17:57.160
Once she's settled, I'll have her leave.

311
17:57.160 --> 17:58.120
How cold.

312
17:58.120 --> 18:00.480
It's not like I can do any more for her.

313
18:00.480 --> 18:02.290
Ikuru, are you serious?

314
18:02.290 --> 18:05.340
Do you really think she can teach modern elementary schoolers?

315
18:05.340 --> 18:08.360
I guess she'll have to resign.

316
18:08.360 --> 18:09.510
- Ikuru! - Woah!

317
18:09.510 --> 18:13.110
That's horrible! You're going to just let her fail?

318
18:13.110 --> 18:16.220
She can't do it, and that's a fact.

319
18:16.220 --> 18:18.410
But she wants to try.

320
18:18.410 --> 18:19.940
Maybe then she'll give up.

321
18:19.940 --> 18:21.800
Irresponsible.

322
18:21.800 --> 18:23.420
What, you think I have time for...

323
18:23.420 --> 18:26.480
Coward. Give her a hand! Maybe it'll work out!

324
18:26.480 --> 18:29.420
If Ms. Iroha can't go back, she has to live here, you know?

325
18:29.420 --> 18:33.220
That goes for all of us, you and me included.

326
18:34.070 --> 18:36.440
Then tell me, why don't you go to school?

327
18:36.440 --> 18:38.510
Why do you refuse to attend?

328
18:38.510 --> 18:40.870
We're not talking about me right now.

329
18:40.870 --> 18:45.140
You ran, because reality didn't live up to your ideals.

330
18:45.140 --> 18:47.000
Everyone's in a similar boat.

331
18:47.000 --> 18:49.190
To make your ideals real, they first have to be possible.

332
18:49.190 --> 18:51.580
And if they're not, we either give up, or quit.

333
18:52.560 --> 18:54.330
In other words...

334
18:55.860 --> 18:58.360
You're going to abandon her?

335
18:58.360 --> 19:00.210
You're the worst.

336
19:02.000 --> 19:03.640
That's right.

337
19:03.640 --> 19:07.000
People everywhere are suffering to some degree.

338
19:09.970 --> 19:13.790
We have no time to spare on the pain of others.

339
19:33.670 --> 19:36.280
So it wasn't a dream.

340
19:40.590 --> 19:41.990
You're heading out?

341
19:41.990 --> 19:43.590
What about breakfast?

342
19:43.590 --> 19:45.090
I'll eat out today.

343
19:45.090 --> 19:47.840
At least bring a rice ball with you.

344
19:47.840 --> 19:50.420
Hold on, I'll cook some rice.

345
19:51.020 --> 19:54.270
I'm fine. You don't even know how to use the rice cooker.

346
19:54.270 --> 19:55.720
Then I'll learn.

347
19:55.720 --> 19:59.320
I can't have you setting fires left and right.

348
20:01.430 --> 20:04.170
Sorry. I'm running late.

349
20:04.170 --> 20:05.860
Hey.

350
20:07.480 --> 20:10.990
This is fine.

351
20:10.990 --> 20:15.200
I decided my motto, didn't I?

352
20:19.310 --> 20:23.830
[Not my problem]

353
20:23.830 --> 20:25.030
"Not my problem"!

354
20:25.030 --> 20:27.610
[Not my problem]

355
20:28.810 --> 20:30.410
Please recharge.

356
20:30.410 --> 20:32.370
- Who? - To set back on standby,

357
20:32.370 --> 20:36.090
- What the... - please press the start button.

358
20:36.990 --> 20:39.410
The hell?

359
20:41.010 --> 20:43.460
Their mother?

360
21:04.060 --> 21:07.570
At least the sun is still the same.

361
21:09.040 --> 21:11.450
People are living their lives.

362
21:11.450 --> 21:13.840
There are houses, and towns, too.

363
21:13.840 --> 21:15.890
Nothing has changed.

364
21:21.650 --> 21:24.700
Mount Fuji!

365
21:31.360 --> 21:35.280
[May 7th, 7AM]

366
21:35.280 --> 21:37.730
Alright.

367
21:42.060 --> 21:43.840
See you later.

368
21:49.570 --> 21:52.890
Good morning, Mr. Ichinose.

369
21:52.890 --> 21:55.670
Huh? Ms. Nashiki?

370
21:55.670 --> 21:57.330
You're back?

371
22:00.980 --> 22:02.860
Missus Saya... I mean,

372
22:02.860 --> 22:06.950
Saya helped me practice.

373
22:08.030 --> 22:13.290
My name is Iroha Nashiki... Got that?

374
22:13.290 --> 22:15.430
- Terrifying. - Huh?

375
22:15.430 --> 22:17.880
You're doing great. Now, repeat after me.

376
22:17.880 --> 22:19.750
- Iroha. - Iroha.

377
22:19.750 --> 22:21.250
- Saya. - Saya.

378
22:21.250 --> 22:22.460
- Ikuru. - Ikuru.

379
22:22.460 --> 22:23.800
- Hey! - Me.

380
22:23.800 --> 22:25.240
- Me. - You.

381
22:25.240 --> 22:26.370
- You. - That pleb.

382
22:26.370 --> 22:28.340
- That pleb. - What are you teaching her?

383
22:28.340 --> 22:30.330
And one more thing. Here.

384
22:30.330 --> 22:31.510
For good measure.

385
22:31.510 --> 22:34.490
It's something I used in elementary school.

386
22:35.330 --> 22:37.390
I registered my number,

387
22:37.390 --> 22:40.960
so press here, and I'll answer right away.

388
22:40.960 --> 22:42.250
No matter where we are?

389
22:42.250 --> 22:46.570
Yup. And no matter how far apart we are.

390
22:49.640 --> 22:52.800
So couriers aren't needed anymore.

391
22:54.180 --> 22:58.420
If my father saw this, he'd go red with rage.

392
22:58.420 --> 23:01.160
Well, uh...

393
23:01.160 --> 23:03.230
But some things never change, do they?

394
23:03.230 --> 23:06.540
People want to be connected, no matter the age.

395
23:06.540 --> 23:07.860
Exactly!

396
23:07.860 --> 23:11.260
So don't be scared, okay?

397
23:11.260 --> 23:13.060
Come here, I'll tie your hair.

398
23:13.060 --> 23:15.290
Thanks.

399
23:18.130 --> 23:20.000
We'll be getting on that thing.

400
23:23.240 --> 23:26.600
Woah! What the hell is this?

401
23:26.600 --> 23:28.970
The doors are now closing.

402
23:31.890 --> 23:33.790
Ms. Nashiki, over here.

403
23:33.790 --> 23:35.320
Thanks.

404
23:42.170 --> 23:44.250
Yo. Did you eat breakfast?

405
23:44.250 --> 23:45.660
- Pardon? - Sorry!

406
23:45.660 --> 23:47.450
No talking to strangers.

407
23:47.450 --> 23:49.800
- Why not? - Because it's weird!

408
23:49.800 --> 23:51.510
Why?

409
23:51.510 --> 23:54.760
- Is making conversation weird? - Just shut up! Shush!

410
23:56.760 --> 23:58.390
Sorry.

411
24:08.450 --> 24:10.200
Here we are.

412
24:12.970 --> 24:15.670
It's huge!

413
24:15.670 --> 24:18.050
Our school has three classes per year,

414
24:18.050 --> 24:22.610
and only 459 students, despite being smack-dab in the middle of Shibuya.

415
24:22.610 --> 24:25.970
459 students?

416
24:28.720 --> 24:30.550
I'll be fine.

417
24:31.400 --> 24:34.600
I've been dreaming of this day for ages.

418
24:36.410 --> 24:37.440
Let's go!

419
24:37.440 --> 24:39.370
W-Wait!

420
24:40.300 --> 24:42.860
- I'll explain this at the very least. - Okay.

421
24:42.860 --> 24:45.800
School is an organization, and hierarchy is its lifeblood.

422
24:45.800 --> 24:46.820
- Organization? - Yes.

423
24:46.820 --> 24:49.610
From the top, there's the Principal, Vice Principal, Head of School Affairs,

424
24:49.610 --> 24:51.190
Head of Year, and homeroom teachers.

425
24:51.190 --> 24:54.530
Then separately, there's the Ministry, Board of Education, and PTA.

426
24:54.530 --> 24:57.320
- Wait... - Okay, how about this?

427
24:57.320 --> 25:00.380
Principal equals daimyo. Vice principal, the chief retainer.

428
25:00.380 --> 25:03.240
Head of School Affairs, the steward.

429
25:03.240 --> 25:06.990
Head of Year is a commander.

430
25:06.990 --> 25:09.200
While homeroom teachers are overseers.

431
25:09.200 --> 25:11.440
And there are also outside powers.

432
25:11.440 --> 25:13.700
The Ministry is the shogunate.

433
25:13.700 --> 25:15.780
- The shogunate? - That's right.

434
25:15.780 --> 25:16.870
- Good morning. - Morning.

435
25:16.870 --> 25:19.430
- Good morning. - Morning.

436
25:20.540 --> 25:24.910
Yikes, Ms. Sakurai is coming. Ms. Nashiki, hurry!

437
25:26.270 --> 25:28.570
The Board of Education are managers of the daimyo's Edo residence.

438
25:28.570 --> 25:31.390
The PTA is a gathering of wealthy merchants, or...

439
25:31.390 --> 25:33.040
town elders.

440
25:33.040 --> 25:36.010
The children are citizens. While we teachers are, uh...

441
25:36.010 --> 25:37.400
retainers!

442
25:37.400 --> 25:39.280
And retainers must obey the daimyo and shogunate, right?

443
25:39.280 --> 25:40.900
Of course.

444
25:40.900 --> 25:42.300
Good.

445
25:42.950 --> 25:45.570
- Ready? - Yeah.

446
25:46.480 --> 25:47.870
Good morning.

447
25:47.870 --> 25:49.620
- Good morning. - Morning.

448
25:49.620 --> 25:51.790
- Morning. - Hey!

449
25:51.790 --> 25:53.350
Too short a break, huh?

450
25:53.350 --> 25:56.000
My Golden Week wasn't "golden" at all.

451
25:56.000 --> 25:59.220
- Good morning. - Morning.

452
25:59.220 --> 26:01.110
How many days till summer break?

453
26:01.110 --> 26:03.430
Come on.

454
26:04.330 --> 26:09.140
Good morning to you all, fellow comrades!

455
26:09.140 --> 26:10.650
Huh?

456
26:14.380 --> 26:16.400
What are you doing? Stand up!

457
26:16.400 --> 26:19.160
- I'm respecting them. - Really, a joke?

458
26:19.160 --> 26:21.890
A joke, first thing after break?

459
26:21.890 --> 26:24.900
That wasn't funny at all.

460
26:26.570 --> 26:29.170
- Principal Tsukamoto! Good morning! - Good morning.

461
26:29.170 --> 26:30.370
Madame!

462
26:30.370 --> 26:32.120
Stop that! Stand!

463
26:32.120 --> 26:34.170
- Good morning. - Good morning.

464
26:34.170 --> 26:35.920
- Morning. Morning! - Alright.

465
26:35.920 --> 26:38.470
- Golden Week has come and gone once more. - Hurry.

466
26:38.470 --> 26:40.480
Sit there. There!

467
26:40.480 --> 26:44.080
Students will avoid school, and be unmotivated after break.

468
26:44.080 --> 26:49.040
So let us not forget our three core values:

469
26:49.040 --> 26:51.810
Observe, report, and teamwork.

470
26:51.810 --> 26:54.910
Repeat after me. Observe, report, and teamwork.

471
26:54.910 --> 26:57.490
Observe, report, and teamwork.

472
26:57.490 --> 26:59.560
I don't hear the enthusiasm, folks!

473
26:59.560 --> 27:00.880
Once again.

474
27:00.880 --> 27:03.080
- Year three, class three. - Observe, report, and teamwork.

475
27:03.080 --> 27:05.170
Observe, report, and teamwork.

476
27:05.170 --> 27:07.490
- Alright! - Woah!

477
27:07.490 --> 27:10.170
You're raring to go, Ms. Nashiki.

478
27:10.170 --> 27:12.170
- Yes, ma'am! - Ma'am!

479
27:12.170 --> 27:15.980
- Oh god... - I wish you all the best of luck.

480
27:15.980 --> 27:18.940
- Thank you. - Thank you, ma'am.

481
27:21.060 --> 27:22.820
Ms. Nashiki.

482
27:22.820 --> 27:25.120
- What happened? - Huh?

483
27:25.120 --> 27:28.080
I mean, you seem very different.

484
27:28.080 --> 27:29.120
What?

485
27:29.120 --> 27:33.880
Ms. Nashiki. Let's keep it simple. Otherwise we'll all tire out.

486
27:33.880 --> 27:35.390
Yes, ma'am.

487
27:35.990 --> 27:38.800
It'll only be a day.

488
27:38.800 --> 27:41.760
Alright, time to head out.

489
27:47.380 --> 27:51.950
One day, and everything will be over.

490
27:51.950 --> 27:55.000
Good morning!

491
27:55.000 --> 27:57.390
Hurry, you'll be late!

492
27:57.390 --> 27:58.950
Your classroom is in the very back.

493
27:58.950 --> 28:00.450
Right.

494
28:01.730 --> 28:04.420
- Good morning! - Morning!

495
28:04.420 --> 28:05.880
You boys have got gusto.

496
28:05.880 --> 28:07.590
What's with you, Ms. Nashiki?

497
28:07.590 --> 28:09.360
- Huh? - No dawdling,

498
28:09.360 --> 28:11.180
you'll be late!

499
28:13.290 --> 28:15.110
Morning.

500
28:15.110 --> 28:16.750
Get to your seats, everyone.

501
28:16.750 --> 28:19.590
Yes, Mr. Majima.

502
28:19.590 --> 28:21.240
Alright.

503
28:21.240 --> 28:23.390
Did you all enjoy your Golden Week?

504
28:23.390 --> 28:25.700
Yes.

505
28:25.700 --> 28:27.900
I spent break playing soccer with my friends.

506
28:27.900 --> 28:30.760
- Woah! - With who?

507
28:32.170 --> 28:34.170
2 minutes, 16 seconds.

508
28:34.170 --> 28:37.550
That's how long it took for you all to settle down.

509
28:37.550 --> 28:39.610
- Mr. Takagi. - Yes, Ms. Akutsu?

510
28:39.610 --> 28:42.820
What do you have to say about wasting everyone's time?

511
28:43.730 --> 28:45.090
I'm sorry.

512
28:45.090 --> 28:46.440
And you, Mr. Mori.

513
28:46.440 --> 28:49.690
If you're so sorry, why do it at all?

514
29:06.540 --> 29:08.650
Good morning!

515
29:13.090 --> 29:15.620
Good morning!

516
29:47.300 --> 29:49.900
"To subdue one's self and return to propriety, is perfect virtue".

517
29:49.900 --> 29:51.190
- Huh? - What?

518
29:51.190 --> 29:53.040
These are the words of Confucius.

519
29:53.040 --> 29:58.610
Propriety is not a means to protect oneself from outside forces.

520
29:58.610 --> 30:02.760
Rather, it is a way to discipline one's heart.

521
30:02.760 --> 30:05.650
One does not conform for the sake of others.

522
30:05.650 --> 30:10.660
One conforms to reform oneself.

523
30:11.440 --> 30:13.000
- What's wrong with her? - What?

524
30:13.000 --> 30:17.420
I look forward to teaching you all.

525
30:19.130 --> 30:20.520
What's going on?

526
30:20.520 --> 30:23.330
She's being weird.

527
30:25.210 --> 30:26.920
To call my break eventful

528
30:26.920 --> 30:29.710
is quite the understatement.

529
30:29.710 --> 30:33.920
So while it may seem strange,

530
30:33.920 --> 30:36.120
I ask you all to place these on your desks.

531
30:36.120 --> 30:38.410
Isn't Ms. Nashiki acting weird?

532
30:38.410 --> 30:41.020
Come get your papers as I read them out.

533
30:41.980 --> 30:43.730
Makoto Aizawa.

534
30:43.730 --> 30:45.370
You must be Kenjiro.

535
30:45.370 --> 30:47.280
Nice to meet you.

536
30:48.170 --> 30:50.050
Great.

537
30:50.050 --> 30:52.670
Now I can associate every face with a name.

538
30:52.670 --> 30:54.550
Ms. Nashiki, you meanie!

539
30:54.550 --> 30:58.360
My name isn't "Mariso", it's "Marin Jain"!

540
30:58.360 --> 30:59.970
She wrote your name wrong!

541
30:59.970 --> 31:02.360
"Mariso Jaiso"? What a weird name.

542
31:02.360 --> 31:03.680
Sounds like a rascal's name.

543
31:03.680 --> 31:06.770
- Yeah! - Boys, don't say that!

544
31:06.770 --> 31:09.020
Silence!

545
31:16.450 --> 31:18.520
My deepest apologies to you.

546
31:18.520 --> 31:23.370
Getting a name wrong is an unforgivable crime.

547
31:23.370 --> 31:25.850
Ms. Nashiki?

548
31:25.850 --> 31:28.820
Let me be honest with you.

549
31:28.820 --> 31:30.640
I need you all to listen as well.

550
31:30.640 --> 31:31.890
Yes, Ms. Nashiki.

551
31:31.890 --> 31:33.840
Truth be told,

552
31:33.840 --> 31:36.320
I do badly with katakana. (T/N: A writing style)

553
31:36.320 --> 31:37.940
What?

554
31:37.940 --> 31:39.780
Really? With katakana?

555
31:39.780 --> 31:43.450
Yeah. I never really used it before.

556
31:43.450 --> 31:45.100
- What? - How?

557
31:45.100 --> 31:47.960
I haven't had enough practice with it.

558
31:50.720 --> 31:53.780
These ones especially give me trouble.

559
31:54.880 --> 31:56.380
"So"...

560
31:56.380 --> 31:57.740
And?

561
31:57.740 --> 31:58.780
"N".

562
31:58.780 --> 32:00.800
These ones, too.

563
32:02.560 --> 32:03.930
"Shi".

564
32:03.930 --> 32:05.200
And...

565
32:05.200 --> 32:07.650
- "Tsu"? - And also...

566
32:07.650 --> 32:08.940
And hiragana.

567
32:08.940 --> 32:11.860
Now that's an entirely separate beast. [Yu]

568
32:11.860 --> 32:14.400
Knock it off, Ms. Nashiki. [Yu]

569
32:18.730 --> 32:20.920
The katakana script...

570
32:23.960 --> 32:26.410
derives from Chinese characters.

571
32:28.300 --> 32:29.880
Woah.

572
32:29.880 --> 32:31.780
You there, you're smart.

573
32:31.780 --> 32:34.760
- You could use my name. - Right.

574
32:34.760 --> 32:36.530
Sorry about that...

575
32:39.160 --> 32:42.220
Ichika.

576
32:42.220 --> 32:44.650
Then what about "wo"?

577
32:44.650 --> 32:47.570
What Chinese character does that come from?

578
32:47.570 --> 32:49.450
I... I don't know.

579
32:49.450 --> 32:52.340
Hey, I want to know, too!

580
32:52.340 --> 32:55.280
Pipe down! Do your worksheets!

581
32:55.280 --> 32:58.220
Your worksheets! Sit down.

582
33:00.880 --> 33:02.650
What?

583
33:03.630 --> 33:04.990
Hey, wait up!

584
33:04.990 --> 33:09.030
Where are you guys going?

585
33:10.180 --> 33:14.090
Over here? Hey, wait!

586
33:30.370 --> 33:33.740
Struggle to complete it, and you never will.

587
33:33.740 --> 33:36.940
Fun is the path to knowledge.

588
33:36.940 --> 33:38.910
Yes, Master.

589
33:40.720 --> 33:42.350
Ms. Nashiki, hurry!

590
33:42.350 --> 33:43.820
- Be right there. - Hurry!

591
33:43.820 --> 33:45.380
Alright.

592
33:45.380 --> 33:47.380
Found something already?

593
33:58.800 --> 34:00.060
What're you guys up to?

594
34:00.060 --> 34:03.220
Look, we found something interesting!

595
34:03.220 --> 34:04.330
Look here.

596
34:04.330 --> 34:05.610
Apparently, "sa" is from "san"!

597
34:05.610 --> 34:08.140
- Really? - No way.

598
34:08.140 --> 34:10.060
How does "he" come from "bu"?

599
34:10.060 --> 34:11.470
It's read as "oozato".

600
34:11.470 --> 34:13.990
But how does "oozato"

601
34:13.990 --> 34:15.250
- become "he"? - Ms. Nashiki, look!

602
34:15.250 --> 34:17.310
"Te" comes from "ten"!

603
34:17.310 --> 34:19.490
You found a good one, Hinata!

604
34:19.490 --> 34:21.860
Everyone, listen up!

605
34:21.860 --> 34:24.430
I heard a commotion over in her class.

606
34:24.430 --> 34:26.550
She's been acting strange all day today.

607
34:26.550 --> 34:29.930
I heard something about the library as well.

608
34:29.930 --> 34:31.480
What are you doing?

609
34:31.480 --> 34:34.370
Nothing. Just admiring the weather.

610
34:34.370 --> 34:36.010
I see. Mind if I get past you there?

611
34:36.010 --> 34:38.180
- How's your health? - Fine.

612
34:38.180 --> 34:40.850
Excuse me.

613
34:40.850 --> 34:42.710
Class 3?

614
34:42.710 --> 34:45.630
Look above, and you'll always see it.

615
34:45.630 --> 34:47.000
- What's that? - The sky!

616
34:47.000 --> 34:49.510
Exactly. The sky.

617
34:49.510 --> 34:53.430
And that celestial body up there uses the same character.

618
34:53.430 --> 34:55.230
Celestial body?

619
34:55.230 --> 34:58.120
- I think she means the sun. - You got it.

620
34:58.120 --> 35:01.040
- The sun is the same... - What are you kids doing?

621
35:01.040 --> 35:02.180
It's recess right now.

622
35:02.180 --> 35:05.370
Ms. Akutsu! I'm interested in Chinese characters now!

623
35:05.370 --> 35:09.820
It's like I'm learning brand new characters, even though I'm not!

624
35:12.520 --> 35:16.660
Huh? That's the bell to end recess.

625
35:17.740 --> 35:19.870
- What's up? - Hurry!

626
35:19.870 --> 35:21.470
- Why? Where's everyone going? - Ms. Nashiki, come on!

627
35:21.470 --> 35:23.230
Alright, I'm coming.

628
35:23.230 --> 35:25.860
Don't forget your things!

629
35:25.860 --> 35:28.310
No running in the halls!

630
35:29.880 --> 35:32.270
Ms. Nashiki.

631
35:32.270 --> 35:36.150
Where did you discover this method of teaching?

632
35:36.150 --> 35:38.020
- Huh? - I mean,

633
35:38.020 --> 35:40.460
it's quite... unique.

634
35:40.460 --> 35:43.870
You must make sure to separate recess and class time.

635
35:43.870 --> 35:45.340
It messes with discipline.

636
35:45.340 --> 35:47.920
Yes, ma'am. Sorry.

637
35:52.190 --> 35:54.740
Aw, man.

638
36:13.290 --> 36:16.050
She taught a class.

639
36:16.050 --> 36:18.820
She taught, using her own methods.

640
36:21.740 --> 36:23.810
Wanna go to the park?

641
36:23.810 --> 36:24.990
Aw, I wanna play indoors.

642
36:24.990 --> 36:28.030
I don't think you can come over today.

643
36:30.140 --> 36:32.350
We're 2-to-3 now.

644
36:32.350 --> 36:34.530
- Yeah. - Dude, watch out.

645
36:34.530 --> 36:36.650
You guys are in the way.

646
36:39.030 --> 36:44.710
He touched her! He touched her!

647
36:44.710 --> 36:46.360
He touched her! [Not my problem]

648
36:49.260 --> 36:50.710
What sort of hit was that?

649
36:50.710 --> 36:52.470
Try again.

650
37:03.650 --> 37:06.510
Hey, you two. Stop.

651
37:06.510 --> 37:08.320
We're not bothering anyone.

652
37:08.320 --> 37:10.320
- Hey, that was scary. - You're already fourth graders.

653
37:10.320 --> 37:12.140
It's fine, Mr. Ichinose.

654
37:12.140 --> 37:14.150
Quit messing around.

655
37:15.080 --> 37:16.790
Get cleaning, you two.

656
37:16.790 --> 37:18.750
Yes, Ms. Nashiki.

657
37:20.180 --> 37:21.650
- Stop it. - It's fine,

658
37:21.650 --> 37:23.430
- shut up already. - You'll hurt someone.

659
37:23.430 --> 37:25.740
It'll be fine.

660
37:30.890 --> 37:33.130
- Ready? - Yeah.

661
37:37.990 --> 37:40.130
Enough!

662
37:44.420 --> 37:46.250
Watch out!

663
37:55.360 --> 37:57.150
Are you okay?

664
37:57.810 --> 38:00.610
Are you okay? You aren't hurt?

665
38:00.610 --> 38:02.040
I'm so sorry.

666
38:02.040 --> 38:04.410
- Are you hurt? - What's wrong?

667
38:05.230 --> 38:07.300
Oh crap.

668
38:09.020 --> 38:10.770
Hey.

669
38:14.270 --> 38:16.080
- Get over here. - Let me go!

670
38:16.080 --> 38:18.580
I'm so sorry.

671
38:18.580 --> 38:22.880
We'll have to tell her parents the truth,

672
38:22.880 --> 38:24.710
and apologize profusely to them.

673
38:24.710 --> 38:27.730
Right. The responsibility was mine.

674
38:27.730 --> 38:30.220
I will go apologize to them.

675
38:30.220 --> 38:36.250
In this case, a student accidentally flung a broom,

676
38:36.250 --> 38:39.750
causing a window to shatter.

677
38:40.720 --> 38:46.500
Strictly speaking, it's not your fault.

678
38:48.210 --> 38:53.910
However, due to issues you faced at your previous schools...

679
38:56.060 --> 39:02.110
I don't believe you caused any harassment, or used physical punishment.

680
39:03.610 --> 39:06.050
I believe every incident was a misunderstanding.

681
39:06.050 --> 39:08.560
You are a serious individual, after all.

682
39:09.530 --> 39:11.050
Which is exactly why I ask

683
39:11.050 --> 39:16.280
that you pull yourself together, so you are not misunderstood again.

684
39:21.570 --> 39:23.700
Thank you.

685
39:30.770 --> 39:32.910
What?

686
39:32.910 --> 39:36.010
Why do you have to apologize?

687
39:42.460 --> 39:44.410
You two...

688
39:44.410 --> 39:47.330
This incident was their fault alone.

689
39:50.520 --> 39:52.490
- Hey, stop! - Let go!

690
39:52.490 --> 39:54.510
What's your deal? You teach third grade, not us!

691
39:54.510 --> 39:56.240
Silence!

692
39:58.450 --> 40:01.150
"Clean, handle, conduct".

693
40:01.150 --> 40:05.820
To clean. To handle people. To know conduct.

694
40:05.820 --> 40:10.700
These are the three pillars of being human.

695
40:10.700 --> 40:12.110
Being human?

696
40:12.110 --> 40:18.350
Disregarding discipline can be life or death in a warrior household.

697
40:19.490 --> 40:22.960
Those who do not properly use their tools,

698
40:22.960 --> 40:26.050
are punished for their sloppy nature.

699
40:26.050 --> 40:28.920
Brooms, sickles,

700
40:28.920 --> 40:31.970
both transform, depending on their uses, like so.

701
40:39.110 --> 40:40.680
We're sorry.

702
40:40.680 --> 40:42.170
We're sorry.

703
40:42.170 --> 40:43.610
What?

704
40:43.610 --> 40:46.760
The teachers aren't to blame.

705
40:46.760 --> 40:49.870
Their parents ought to teach them better discipline.

706
40:49.870 --> 40:51.790
Ms. Nashiki.

707
40:59.610 --> 41:03.110
Suzuki. Kudo.

708
41:03.110 --> 41:05.340
Thanks for apologizing.

709
41:06.560 --> 41:08.680
Be careful in the halls from now on, okay?

710
41:12.230 --> 41:14.070
You two can go now.

711
41:18.560 --> 41:21.200
Why? You won't tell their parents?

712
41:21.200 --> 41:23.240
Don't meddle any further.

713
41:24.800 --> 41:27.620
What you say is right.

714
41:27.620 --> 41:31.910
But nowadays, what's factually right

715
41:31.910 --> 41:35.780
doesn't necessarily come across as being correct.

716
41:38.110 --> 41:40.940
Teachers are never just.

717
41:47.240 --> 41:49.230
So you had no class today?

718
41:49.230 --> 41:50.830
No, we did.

719
41:50.830 --> 41:53.450
- We went to the library, and... - That's self-studying.

720
41:53.450 --> 41:55.170
Did your teacher not teach?

721
41:55.170 --> 41:56.780
No, Mom. She...

722
41:56.780 --> 42:00.060
Preparation for middle school exams start in third grade.

723
42:00.060 --> 42:03.150
I wonder if the other moms know of this.

724
42:03.730 --> 42:07.330
Daichi. You'll be late for cram school.

725
42:07.330 --> 42:09.510
- Okay. - I left your bag there.

726
42:09.510 --> 42:11.200
Thanks.

727
42:11.810 --> 42:14.790
[Did you hear about Ms. Nashiki today?] [She's being so irresponsible.]

728
42:35.560 --> 42:37.220
Ikuru?

729
42:38.550 --> 42:40.220
Hey, Ikuru!

730
42:43.780 --> 42:46.800
I wasn't waiting for you.

731
42:53.480 --> 42:55.610
Hey.

732
42:55.610 --> 42:57.580
What did you mean by that earlier?

733
42:58.780 --> 43:01.620
About teachers not ever being just?

734
43:03.870 --> 43:05.320
I meant it quite literally.

735
43:05.320 --> 43:09.450
Like how a huge bonfire can start from nothing.

736
43:09.450 --> 43:10.910
That doesn't make sense.

737
43:10.910 --> 43:13.250
Obviously someone set the flame first.

738
43:13.250 --> 43:15.110
I'm sure there is a culprit.

739
43:15.110 --> 43:17.950
But what use is there in exposing them?

740
43:17.950 --> 43:20.680
The culprits are the student's parents.

741
43:20.680 --> 43:23.070
You're lucky, Ms. Iroha.

742
43:23.070 --> 43:27.180
You know a time where teachers are respected above all.

743
43:27.860 --> 43:29.680
Are you saying it's different now?

744
43:29.680 --> 43:31.740
Unfortunately, yes.

745
43:31.740 --> 43:35.700
To be frank with you, my kids look down on me.

746
43:35.700 --> 43:39.140
I can't argue against their parents either.

747
43:39.140 --> 43:43.900
Then why did you become a teacher?

748
43:45.610 --> 43:49.030
How can you prepare yourself for what's to come every day?

749
43:49.030 --> 43:53.760
Isn't it because you want to become your version of an ideal teacher?

750
43:53.760 --> 43:55.560
I suppose so.

751
43:55.560 --> 43:58.450
But if I only followed my ideals,

752
43:58.450 --> 44:01.030
I'd never get anywhere.

753
44:01.030 --> 44:05.530
In the game of life, I'd have negative points.

754
44:06.460 --> 44:10.820
That's why I choose to accomplish the bare minimum every day.

755
44:10.820 --> 44:13.680
The bare minimum?

756
44:13.680 --> 44:17.710
To protect the lives of my students.

757
44:21.290 --> 44:22.740
It's not a grand thing, really.

758
44:22.740 --> 44:25.470
Modern technology may make things convenient,

759
44:25.470 --> 44:29.060
but that doesn't mean life is any easier to live.

760
44:31.250 --> 44:34.730
That's why I want to protect the lives of not only my own students,

761
44:34.730 --> 44:40.110
but all students of Shibuya Third, including those who don't attend school.

762
44:40.110 --> 44:45.680
I guess that's my absolute, ultimate goal I won't budge on.

763
44:53.470 --> 44:57.610
[Come, and you have a date.] [You have 15 minutes.]

764
45:00.410 --> 45:03.940
Sorry, I bet that sounded nerdy.

765
45:03.940 --> 45:05.890
"N-Nerdy"?

766
45:05.890 --> 45:08.840
Absolute, ultimate... Pretty cringe, right?

767
45:08.840 --> 45:10.600
Cringe?

768
45:10.600 --> 45:13.130
Is that a bad thing?

769
45:13.130 --> 45:16.510
Yes. It's a terrible thing to be afflicted with.

770
45:16.510 --> 45:18.930
Being cringe can ruin your life.

771
45:18.930 --> 45:20.350
But enough about me.

772
45:20.350 --> 45:22.120
Huh?

773
45:22.120 --> 45:24.070
I didn't get a word you said.

774
45:24.070 --> 45:26.970
Neither did I.

775
45:27.810 --> 45:30.550
But you know,

776
45:30.550 --> 45:32.490
you're a cool guy.

777
45:33.910 --> 45:35.380
Huh?

778
45:36.510 --> 45:38.350
You're cool.

779
45:39.180 --> 45:40.670
Huh?

780
45:56.400 --> 46:00.830
Please leave a message after the tone.

781
46:01.640 --> 46:04.550
Ikuru, are you still at school?

782
46:04.550 --> 46:07.070
Or...

783
46:07.070 --> 46:09.450
Are you with someone?

784
46:09.450 --> 46:12.050
"Cool"?

785
46:15.030 --> 46:16.940
Me?
